From 850d488dfa5781697b9fbdbe7b5956df09216bea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Hagadorn <jeff@aletheia.io>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 10:29:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] smu: add Strix Halo PM table version 0x64010C

The ONEXPLAYER X2Mini PRO (Ryzen AI MAX+ 388, SMU v10.100.6.0) reports PM
table version 0x64010C, which is absent from the Strix Halo size table.
Probing fails with:

    ryzen_smu: Unknown PM table version: 0x0064010C
    ryzen_smu: Failed to probe the PM table -- disabling feature (249)

leaving pm_table, pm_table_size and pm_table_version unexposed. That costs
more than read-back: with ryzen_smu loaded but unable to probe, ryzenadj
fails at init with "Unable to get os_access Obj, check permission", which
reads like a permissions problem and is not.

The version differs from the already-supported 0x64020C only in the middle
byte, and the same 0xE50 size applies. Verified on hardware: after writing
distinct limits via MP1 messages 0x14 / 0x15 / 0x16 (stapm 31 W, fast 53 W,
slow 47 W), the table reads back

    offset 0x0  = 31.000002   (STAPM limit)
    offset 0x8  = 53.000004   (PPT limit fast)
    offset 0x10 = 47.000004   (PPT limit slow)

matching the documented layout, and `ryzenadj -i` reports the same values
independently.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Hagadorn <jeff@aletheia.io>
---
 smu.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smu.c b/smu.c
index 6eae6dc..3636bb6 100644
--- a/smu.c
+++ b/smu.c
@@ -1153,6 +1153,12 @@ u32 smu_update_pmtable_size(u32 version) {
     break;
   case CODENAME_STRIXHALO:
     switch (version) {
+    // 0x64010C is the ONEXPLAYER X2Mini PRO (Ryzen AI MAX+ 388, SMU
+    // v10.100.6.0). It differs from 0x64020C only in the middle byte and takes
+    // the same size, which is not published by AMD and was validated on
+    // hardware: after writing distinct limits via MP1 messages 0x14/0x15/0x16,
+    // the stapm/fast/slow floats at offsets 0x0/0x8/0x10 read them back.
+    case 0x64010C:
     case 0x64020C:
       g_smu.pm_dram_map_size = 0xE50;
       break;
-- 
2.55.0

